docs/bilinear_interpolation.html
docs/ml_pipeline_explorer.html

# ---- Teaching material ----
# Six ML labs that rebuild experiment.py in miniature on the real 612-row panel,
# plus the grader they feed. They are study material, not part of the analysis:
# nothing in src/, scripts/ or the paper imports them, and no result depends on
# them. Their narrative half already lives in ../learning-centre/surrey/, so
# keeping the notebooks here left a teaching apparatus split across two repos
# and put coursework in a research compendium.
#
# They stay on disk and still run, because they import src.pipeline and read
# data/processed/features.parquet and would break anywhere else.
notebooks/labs/

# ---- Manuscript ----
# Source is tracked; build artifacts are not. The whole directory was ignored
# until 2026-08-12 on the reasoning below, which was sound about publishing and
# wrong about versioning: this manuscript has had its central result corrected
# four times, each correction propagated by hand across two .tex files, and one
# of those passes exists only to record that an earlier "propagation done" note
# was false. An unversioned main.tex is precisely the failure history catches.
#
# ⚠️ THE REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC AND THE PREPRINT IS NOT POSTED. Tracking the
# source means the next push publishes the manuscript, ahead of the preprint and
# against the hold that is still in force. Commit freely; do not push until the
# preprint is up. That is the surviving half of the original reasoning:
#
#   "The paper is not published from this repository. It goes to a preprint
#    server; the README links the DOI once posted. Keeping a draft here would
#    put an unposted, still-revising manuscript in public and create a second
#    copy to drift out of sync with the version of record."
#
# Artifacts stay out. _archive/ is 7.6M of a 13M tree and holds the dead
# monolith, which CLAUDE.md forbids editing or quoting. The figures are excluded
# too, so a fresh clone does NOT build until they are regenerated.
# Private correspondence, not manuscript source. The APC waiver enquiry states
# the author has no employer, no grant and is a secondary-school student. That
# is fine to send an editorial office and is not something a public repository
# should carry. Remove this line if you want it tracked.
docs/papers/waiver_enquiry_MEE.md

# Process, not product. These are inputs to how the manuscript was made: prompts,
# completed plans, an AI-generated referee report, and reading checklists. A
# reader arriving from the paper wants the manuscript source and the pipeline;
# a referee reads this kind of file as detritus, and the prompt library in
# particular is not something the repository needs to publish. The AI-use
# disclosure that DOES belong in public is in .zenodo.json and the manuscript.
docs/papers/MEE_DESK_CHECK_PROMPT.md
docs/papers/REFEREE_PASS_RUNBOOK.md
docs/papers/CITATION_TARGETS.md
docs/papers/READING_ORDER.md
docs/papers/SPLIT_PLAN.md
docs/papers/split.py
docs/papers/**/REFEREE_BRIEF.md
docs/papers/paper-a/BLIND_REFEREE_PROMPTS.md
docs/papers/paper-a/VOICE_PASS_PROMPT.md
docs/papers/paper-a/REFRAME_PLAN.md
docs/papers/paper-a/referee_report_paperA.md
docs/papers/GEMINI_GENRE_PROMPT.md
docs/papers/GENRE_REFS_VERIFIED.md
docs/REPO_SLIMMING_RESEARCH_PROMPT.md

# The known-weakness register. Kept local until the preprint is posted, for two
# reasons. It is written as a lab notebook to self, in a register voice that
# judges its own results ("indefensible", "embarrassing rather than
# interesting"), and the reader-facing version of it is the paper's Limitations
# section. And REFEREE_BRIEF.md withholds this list on purpose so an outside
# report can be compared against it afterwards; publishing both in one repo
# defeats that. Revisit once the preprint is up.
docs/papers/KNOWN_ISSUES.md

# ⛔ THE MANUSCRIPTS THEMSELVES, held until the preprint is posted. Pushing these
# would put both unposted papers on a public repository ahead of the preprint
# server, which is the situation the original blanket ignore existed to prevent.
# The bibliographies, build scripts and wordcount.py stay tracked: they carry no
# results, and they keep part of the version control this directory was opened
# up for. DELETE THESE TWO LINES the day the preprint goes up.
docs/papers/**/*.tex

docs/papers/_archive/
docs/papers/**/figures/
docs/papers/**/*.pdf
docs/papers/**/*.zip
docs/papers/**/*.bak
docs/papers/**/*.superseded

# Generated board + poster figure variants. All rebuild in seconds from tracked
# source: `--mode poster`, scripts/plot_board_figures.py, docs/board/build.sh.
# The paper-mode figures in docs/figures/ and docs/deliverable/ stay tracked —
# the manuscript embeds them. The board's fonts are tracked deliberately: without
# them the board renders in a substitute face and is not reproducible.
docs/figures/board/
docs/figures/poster/
docs/deliverable/poster/
docs/board/board.pdf
docs/board/board_preview.png
docs/board/board_detail_300dpi.png

# The Learning Centres moved out of this repository on 2026-08-05 and now live
# in ../learning-centre, which carries its own ignore rules for those extracts.

# Anonymised review archive, rebuilt by scripts/make_anon_archive.sh on demand.
surrey-pipeline-anon.zip
